RER_SETUP_READY http://127.0.0.1:8787
Next: rer dev opens http://127.0.0.1:8787 signed in as the owner; first-run setup finishes at http://127.0.0.1:8787/setup. rer preview prints a one-time native owner link on loopback; rer demo also prints a separate native owner entry.
To host it on your own Cloudflare account later, rer deploy needs:
  - CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID and CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN (Create an account API token at https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens with these account permissions: Workers Scripts: Edit, D1: Edit. Copy your account ID from the Cloudflare dashboard.)
  - MAIL_PROVIDER
  - production sign-in mail: MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS (a real sender on your provider's verified domain; bare address or Display Name <address>), MAIL_PROVIDER_API_KEY or MAIL_PROVIDER_API_KEY (or RESEND_API_KEY), or an approved Auth SSO install
Set them in your environment or a private (mode 0600) file passed with --env-file, then check with rer deploy --dry-run.
